    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0888" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d473-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-03">3 December 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret from the President.</p>
                <p>I think it best not to appoint International Civil Aviation Committee<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d473-f2"/> until I get back because I think you and I should
                    agree on some general principles to lay before them before they meet.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d473-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d473-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the White House Map Room, via military channels, and forwarded by the Map
                    Room to Hull in paraphrase.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d473-f2" n="2" xml:id="d473-f2-content">
                <p>See Hull’s message of November 29, 1943, to
                        Roosevelt, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg621">p. 621</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
